.TH PIQUELCTL 1 "" "piquelctl 0.1.0" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
piquelctl \- command\-line client for piqueld
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpiquelctl\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Operate a piqueld control plane.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl\fR connects to the daemon\*(Aqs Unix socket, \fB/run/piqueld/piqueld.sock\fR, unless \fB\-\-socket\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR, the \fBPIQUELD_SOCKET\fR or \fBPIQUELD_URL\fR variable, or a connection profile names another endpoint. It authenticates with \fBPIQUELD_TOKEN\fR, or with the login that \fBpiquelctl login\fR saved. On the daemon host, root and the daemon\*(Aqs user need no login.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.PP
Every command accepts these options, before or after its own.
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Connect with this profile from the profiles files.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to \fBPIQUELD_PROFILE\fR, else to the profile named by the profiles file\*(Aqs top\-level \fBdefault\fR, else to the profile named \fBdefault\fR if there is one.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-profiles\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read profiles only from this file.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to \fBPIQUELD_PROFILES_FILE\fR. Without either, \fBpiquelctl\fR reads \fB/etc/piqueld/profiles.toml\fR, then \fB~/.config/piqueld/profiles.toml\fR (in \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR when it is set), whose profiles replace those of the same name.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Connect to the daemon\*(Aqs Unix socket at this path.
.RS
.PP
It overrides \fBPIQUELD_SOCKET\fR, \fBPIQUELD_URL\fR and the profile\*(Aqs endpoint. Without any of them, \fBpiquelctl\fR uses \fB/run/piqueld/piqueld.sock\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-account\fR \fI<ACCOUNT>\fR
Act as this saved login, by account ID, or by username ignoring case.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to the login you saved last for this daemon. \fBPIQUELD_TOKEN\fR takes precedence over saved logins.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-insecure\-http\fR
Allow sending credentials over plain HTTP to a remote daemon.
.RS
.PP
Only use it when something else encrypts the connection, such as Tailscale: \fBpiquelctl\fR adds no encryption and doesn\*(Aqt check. HTTPS, loopback addresses and the Unix socket don\*(Aqt need it.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Connect to the daemon over HTTP or HTTPS at this address.
.RS
.PP
Give an origin without a path, query or credentials, such as \fBhttp://127.0.0.1:7845\fR or \fBhttps://piqueld.example.ts.net\fR. It overrides \fBPIQUELD_URL\fR, \fBPIQUELD_SOCKET\fR and the profile\*(Aqs endpoint.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Give up on the command after this long, such as \fB500ms\fR, \fB30s\fR, \fB2m\fR or \fB1h\fR.
.RS
.PP
A number without a unit is seconds. The limit also applies to each request. Confirmation prompts and waiting for an operation don\*(Aqt count towards it, and it doesn\*(Aqt limit the session of \fBapp exec\fR and \fBpreview exec\fR, or how long \fBlogin\fR waits for your approval. \fBPIQUELD_TIMEOUT\fR and a profile\*(Aqs \fBtimeout\fR replace the default. Default: \fB30s\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Stop waiting for an operation after this long, such as \fB5m\fR or \fB1h\fR.
.RS
.PP
A number without a unit is seconds. Each wait, such as for a deployment, gets its own limit. Stopping to wait doesn\*(Aqt cancel the operation: the daemon goes on with it. \fBPIQUELD_WAIT_TIMEOUT\fR replaces the default. Default: \fB15m\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the result as JSON on standard output.
.RS
.PP
Information, warnings and errors on standard error become one JSON object per line.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Hide human\-readable results, information and progress.
.RS
.PP
JSON results, warnings, errors and prompts still appear, and so do secrets shown only once, such as a new token or invitation link.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-noninteractive\fR
Never prompt, even on a terminal.
.RS
.PP
Commands that ask for confirmation then fail unless you pass \fB\-\-yes\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-request\-id\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Make a change to an application, environment or preview safe to run again: it is made only once.
.RS
.PP
Run the same command with the same ID, such as after losing the connection, and the daemon returns the earlier result instead of making the change again, within 24 hours. Secret, notification, account, token and sign\-in commands, and \fBpreview prune\fR, ignore it, so rerunning one makes its change again. Use a new ID, of up to 128 letters, digits, \fB\-\fR, \fB_\fR, \fB.\fR or \fB:\fR, for each command you mean to run. Defaults to \fBPIQUELD_REQUEST_ID\fR, else a new ID each time.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print what a command does and its options: a summary with \fB\-h\fR, everything below with \fB\-\-help\fR.
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print the version of \fBpiquelctl\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBpiquelctl login\fR
Sign in with a passkey through your browser, and save the login.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl logout\fR
Sign out: revoke the current credential and delete its saved copy.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl whoami\fR
Show who you are signed in as and what the current credential may do.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl account\fR
Manage accounts: list, edit and delete them, change their grants and passkeys, and create and revoke invitation and enrollment links.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl token\fR
Create, list and revoke your API tokens and sessions, or revoke an account\*(Aqs.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl audit\fR
Read the audit trail of API requests, newest first.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl recover\-admin\fR
Print a one\-time link that creates a new administrator account.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl sign\-in\-link\fR
Print a one\-time link that signs a browser in as the host operator.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl setup\-link\fR
Print the link that creates the first account.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl profiles\fR
List your connection profiles and their endpoints.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl completions\fR
Print the completion script of a shell.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl secrets\fR
Manage the daemon\*(Aqs encryption key for secrets.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification\fR
Manage notification destinations and their deliveries.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl status\fR
Show whether the daemon responds, its version, and the health of its subsystems.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl resources\fR
Show the daemon process\*(Aqs resource usage, storage, retained history, and queues, measured at most every 5 seconds (requires system:read).
.TP
\fBpiquelctl settings\fR
Show the daemon\*(Aqs effective host settings, read\-only (requires system:read). Change them in its TOML configuration and restart it.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl doctor\fR
Check this CLI\*(Aqs connection and the installation\*(Aqs health.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl dns\fR
Inspect the daemon\*(Aqs DNS providers.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl builder\fR
