.SS
piquelctl login
.PP
Sign in with a passkey through your browser, and save the login.
.PP
\fBlogin\fR prints a link and a code. Open the link in any browser, even on another machine, and approve the code with your passkey. It waits until the code expires, at most 15 minutes, whatever \fB\-\-timeout\fR says. It then saves the login for this daemon in \fB~/.config/piqueld/credentials.json\fR (in \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR when it is set), or in the file \fBPIQUELD_CREDENTIALS_FILE\fR names.
.PP
Grant options limit what the login may do; without them, it has all your account\*(Aqs access. Here \fB\-\-app\fR takes application IDs, not names, which cannot be looked up before signing in.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl login\fR [OPTIONS]
