piquelctl token create
.PP
Create an API token for your account, and print it.
.PP
The token has only the grants you select, with \fB\-\-preset\fR, \fB\-\-permission\fR, or both, and you must hold them. Use it with \fBPIQUELD_TOKEN\fR. Keep it safe: it is printed once and never shown again. An API token can\*(Aqt create tokens. If you last signed in with your passkey more than 2 minutes ago, it asks you to confirm in a browser first.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl token create\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Token name, up to 200 bytes.
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR
Grant the permissions of this preset.
.RS
.TP
\fBread\-only\fR
Read applications, their logs and history.
.TP
\fBdeploy\fR
Read and deploy applications, such as for CI.
.TP
\fBdeveloper\fR
Everything on applications but deleting them, including running commands in them.
.TP
\fBadmin\fR
Every permission, on the selected applications or on the installation.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-permission\fR \fI<PERMISSION>\fR
Grant this permission.
.RS
.PP
Repeat it to grant several.
.TP
\fBadmin\fR
Every ability, including permissions added later.
.TP
\fBapps:read\fR
Read configuration, status, deployments and secret names.
.TP
\fBapps:write\fR
Edit configuration, apply manifests, rename and add environments.
.TP
\fBapps:deploy\fR
Deploy and reconcile environments, create and deploy previews.
.TP
\fBapps:delete\fR
Delete applications, environments and previews.
.TP
\fBpreviews:deploy\fR
Create and deploy previews and read their logs.
.TP
\fBpreviews:delete\fR
Delete and prune previews.
.TP
\fBsecrets:write\fR
Store and delete secret values.
.TP
\fBlogs:read\fR
Read runtime, build and job logs.
.TP
\fBapps:exec\fR
Run commands in running containers, which can read secret values.
.TP
\fBevents:read\fR
Read history, diagnostics and analytics.
.TP
\fBapps:create\fR
Create applications.
.TP
\fBsystem:read\fR
Read daemon configuration, resources, history and notifications.
.TP
\fBsystem:operate\fR
Recover the secret key and retry notifications.
.TP
\fBaccounts:manage\fR
Manage accounts with equal or less access, and invitations.
.TP
\fBaudit:read\fR
Read every account\*(Aqs audit trail.
.TP
\fBtelemetry:grant\fR
Grant environments every application\*(Aqs telemetry.
.TP
\fBnotifications:manage\fR
Manage notification destinations.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR \fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Limit the application permissions to this application.
.RS
.PP
Repeat it to allow several applications. Without it, the permissions apply to every application. Installation\-wide permissions, such as \fBsystem:read\fR, are never limited.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fI<DAYS>\fR
Expire the token after this many days, from 1.
.RS
.PP
The daemon refuses more days than its \fBauth.max_token_days\fR. Default: \fB90\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-expiry\fR
Never expire the token.
.RS
.PP
The daemon refuses it when it sets \fBauth.max_token_days\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-tailnet\fR \fI<USER_OR_TAG>\fR
Accept the token only over the tailnet, from this user\*(Aqs devices or devices with this tag.
.RS
.PP
Give a login name, such as \fBalice@example.com\fR, or a tag, such as \fBtag:ci\fR. The daemon needs its tailnet node or a private dashboard hostname.
.RE
.SS
piquelctl token list
.PP
List the sessions and API tokens of an account, with their grants and expiry.
.PP
Without \fB\-\-user\fR, lists yours.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl token list\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<ACCOUNT>\fR
List this account\*(Aqs instead, by username or ID.
.RS
.PP
Accounts other than yours need \fBaccounts:manage\fR.
.RE
.SS
piquelctl token revoke
.PP
Revoke a session or API token by ID, or every one of an account with \fB\-\-all\fR.
.PP
Give the ID of a credential from \fBtoken list\fR, or of a host operator browser session, from \fBaccount list\fR. Revoking a credential also revokes everything issued through it, in any account: the API tokens, logins, invitation and enrollment links and passkeys it created, the sessions those passkeys signed in, and so on. It reaches them even when credentials in between have since ended.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl token revoke\fR [OPTIONS] [ID]
.TP
\fI[ID]\fR
Credential ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cascade\fR
Revoke only what you name, leaving valid the credentials, links and passkeys issued through what you named.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Revoke every session and API token of an account instead.
.RS
.PP
Without \fB\-\-user\fR, revokes yours, including the login this command uses. An API token or limited login can\*(Aqt revoke its own account\*(Aqs. It also removes the passkeys the account added while signed in, usually all but its first: pass \fB\-\-no\-cascade\fR to keep them.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<ACCOUNT>\fR
Revoke this account\*(Aqs with \fB\-\-all\fR, by username or ID.
.RS
.PP
Accounts other than yours need \fBaccounts:manage\fR and every grant the account has.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt of \fB\-\-all\fR.
.SS
piquelctl audit
.PP
Read the audit trail of API requests, newest first.
.PP
Each line is one request: when it was made, its outcome and status, what it did and to which application or environment, who made it with which credential, and from where. With \fBaudit:read\fR, you see every account\*(Aqs requests. Without it, you see only your own account\*(Aqs, and an API token only its own.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl audit\fR [OPTIONS]
       piquelctl audit <COMMAND>
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<ACCOUNT>\fR
Only show the requests of this account, by username or ID, even a deleted one.
.RS
.PP
Accounts other than yours need \fBaudit:read\fR. Unlike the global \fB\-\-account\fR, it doesn\*(Aqt choose the login you read with.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-credential\fR \fI<CREDENTIAL>\fR
Only show the requests made with this credential ID, from \fBtoken list\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-outcome\fR \fI<OUTCOME>\fR
Only show the requests with this outcome.
.RS
.TP
\fBallowed\fR
Authorized, and succeeded.
.TP
\fBdenied\fR
Refused: missing credentials or permission, or a target hidden from the caller.
.TP
\fBfailed\fR
Authorized, but failed.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fI<CURSOR>\fR
Read the page after this cursor, which the previous page printed.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Show at most this many items, from 1 to 100. Default: \fB50\fR.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl audit verify\fR
Check that no one altered the audit trail.
.SS
piquelctl audit verify
.PP
Check that no one altered the audit trail.
.PP
It checks the trail\*(Aqs hash chain, and exits with code 3 when a record was edited, inserted or removed. It prints the newest link: keep it elsewhere to also detect that the newest records were removed. Needs \fBaudit:read\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl audit verify\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl recover\-admin
.PP
Print a one\-time link that creates a new administrator account.
.PP
Use it to regain access when no administrator can sign in. Run it on the daemon host as root or as the daemon\*(Aqs user, such as with \fBsudo\fR: the daemon serves it only over its Unix socket. The link works once within 24 hours and replaces any earlier one. Issuing it raises a security notification.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl recover\-admin\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl sign\-in\-link
.PP
Print a one\-time link that signs a browser in as the host operator.
.PP
The browser gets full access for 12 hours. The link works once within 10 minutes. Run it on the daemon host as root or as the daemon\*(Aqs user: the daemon serves it only over its Unix socket, to the host operator. It never sends \fBPIQUELD_TOKEN\fR or a saved login. Issuing it raises a security notification.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl sign\-in\-link\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl setup\-link
.PP
Print the link that creates the first account.
.PP
Run it on the daemon host: the daemon serves it only over its Unix socket, and only until the first account exists.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl setup\-link\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-\-open\fR
Also open the link in your default browser.
.SS
piquelctl profiles
.PP
List your connection profiles and their endpoints.
.PP
It reads the profiles files without contacting a daemon, and ignores \fB\-\-profile\fR and the endpoint options.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl profiles\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl completions
.PP
Print the completion script of a shell.
.PP
Save it where your shell loads completions, such as \fBpiquelctl completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/piquelctl\fR. It contacts no daemon.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl completions\fR [OPTIONS] <SHELL>
.TP
\fI<SHELL>\fR
The shell to complete in. Values: \fBbash\fR, \fBelvish\fR, \fBfish\fR, \fBpowershell\fR, \fBzsh\fR.
.SS
piquelctl secrets
.PP
Manage the daemon\*(Aqs encryption key for secrets.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl secrets\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl secrets recover\-key\fR
Recover from a lost secret key by discarding every value it encrypted.
.SS
piquelctl secrets recover\-key
.PP
Recover from a lost secret key by discarding every value it encrypted.
.PP
Use it only when the daemon\*(Aqs \fBsecrets.key\fR is lost and you have no backup: the daemon refuses while the key still works. It discards the stored and generated secret values of ALL applications and environments and the repository webhook secrets, and deletes every notification destination, since their URLs are encrypted. Running services keep their Docker secrets. Afterwards, set the stored secrets again and deploy, which also generates new values for generated secrets, give each repository a new webhook secret with \fBapp repository webhook rotate\fR, and add the notification destinations again with \fBnotification set\fR. Needs \fBsystem:operate\fR. If you last signed in with your passkey more than 2 minutes ago, it asks you to confirm in a browser first.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl secrets recover\-key\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SS
piquelctl notification
.PP
Manage notification destinations and their deliveries.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification list\fR
List notification destinations and what each receives.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification set\fR
Create a notification destination, or change one.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification test\fR
Send a test notification to a destination now.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification delete\fR
Delete a notification destination and cancel its pending deliveries.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification deliveries\fR
List notification deliveries, newest first, with their state, attempts and last error.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl notification retry\fR
Try a failed delivery again now, with the destination\*(Aqs current settings.
.SS
piquelctl notification list
.PP
List notification destinations and what each receives.
.PP
Their URLs are never shown. Needs \fBsystem:read\fR or \fBnotifications:manage\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification list\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl notification set
.PP
Create a notification destination, or change one.
.PP
Options you omit keep the current settings. A new destination needs \fB\-\-url\-file\fR or \fB\-\-url\-stdin\fR. It receives every category but \fBdeployment_succeeded\fR, about every application, without previews. Changing its URL or kind cancels its pending deliveries. Needs \fBnotifications:manage\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification set\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Destination name.
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
Payload format.
.RS
.PP
A new destination defaults to \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fBjson\fR
Versioned JSON describing the event.
.TP
\fBdiscord\fR
A Discord webhook message.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the webhook URL from this file.
.TP
\fB\-\-url\-stdin\fR
Read the webhook URL from standard input. A terminal asks for it without echo.
.TP
\fB\-\-enabled\fR \fI<BOOL>\fR
Whether to send notifications.
.RS
.PP
\fBfalse\fR pauses the destination and cancels its pending deliveries. \fBtrue\fR resumes it, without sending what happened meanwhile. Values: \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-categories\fR \fI<CATEGORIES>\fR
Receive only these categories: comma\-separated, or \fB\*(Aq\*(Aq\fR for none.
.RS
.PP
A category that stays keeps its message. Values: \fBbuild_failures\fR, \fBdeployment_failures\fR, \fBservice_degradation\fR, \fBdaemon_failures\fR, \fBrecovery\fR, \fBsecurity\fR, \fBdaemon_started\fR, \fBdeployment_succeeded\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-message\fR \fI<CATEGORY=TEXT>\fR
Send TEXT with each notification of CATEGORY, and receive that category.
.RS
.PP
TEXT has 1 to 1000 characters, such as a Discord role mention \fB<@&ROLE_ID>\fR. CATEGORY is one of the values \fB\-\-categories\fR accepts. Repeat it for several categories.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-message\fR \fI<CATEGORY>\fR
Stop sending text with this category\*(Aqs notifications.
.RS
.PP
Repeat it for several categories. Values: \fBbuild_failures\fR, \fBdeployment_failures\fR, \fBservice_degradation\fR, \fBdaemon_failures\fR, \fBrecovery\fR, \fBsecurity\fR, \fBdaemon_started\fR, \fBdeployment_succeeded\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-apps\fR \fI<APPS>\fR
Receive notifications only about these applications: comma\-separated names or IDs, or \fB\*(Aq\*(Aq\fR for none.
.RS
.PP
Daemon\-wide notifications, such as daemon failures and security events, arrive either way.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-apps\fR
Receive notifications about every application, including ones created later.
.TP
\fB\-\-previews\fR \fI<BOOL>\fR
Whether to receive notifications about previews. Values: \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR.
.SS
piquelctl notification test
.PP
Send a test notification to a destination now.
.PP
It fails unless the receiver acknowledges it. The test skips the delivery queue and history. Needs \fBnotifications:manage\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification test\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Destination name.
.SS
piquelctl notification delete
.PP
Delete a notification destination and cancel its pending deliveries.
.PP
The delivery history keeps its name. Needs \fBnotifications:manage\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification delete\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Destination name.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SS
piquelctl notification deliveries
.PP
List notification deliveries, newest first, with their state, attempts and last error.
.PP
Needs \fBsystem:read\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification deliveries\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fI<CURSOR>\fR
Read the page after this cursor, which the previous page printed.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Show at most this many items, from 1 to 100. Default: \fB50\fR.
.SS
piquelctl notification retry
.PP
Try a failed delivery again now, with the destination\*(Aqs current settings.
.PP
Needs \fBsystem:operate\fR. The daemon refuses a delivery that hasn\*(Aqt failed or that the destination no longer receives, and says why.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl notification retry\fR [OPTIONS] <ID>
.TP
\fI<ID>\fR
Delivery ID, from \fBnotification deliveries\fR.
.SS
piquelctl status
.PP
Show whether the daemon responds, its version, and the health of its subsystems.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl status\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl resources
.PP
Show the daemon process\*(Aqs resource usage, storage, retained history, and queues, measured at most every 5 seconds (requires system:read).
.PP
\fBpiquelctl resources\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl settings
.PP
Show the daemon\*(Aqs effective host settings, read\-only (requires system:read). Change them in its TOML configuration and restart it.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl settings\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl doctor
.PP
Check this CLI\*(Aqs connection and the installation\*(Aqs health.
.PP
Shows the resolved endpoint and credential, then each daemon check as pass, warn, fail, or skip with a next step. Exits 6 when a check fails.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl doctor\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl dns
.PP
Inspect the daemon\*(Aqs DNS providers.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl dns\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl dns refresh\fR
Check every DNS provider\*(Aqs credentials and zones now.
.SS
piquelctl dns refresh
.PP
Check every DNS provider\*(Aqs credentials and zones now.
.PP
The daemon otherwise checks them every hour. It reads credential files only when it starts, so restart it after changing one. Needs \fBsystem:operate\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl dns refresh\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl builder
.PP
Inspect the build machine images build on.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl builder\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl builder check\fR
Check that the build machine answers now.
.SS
piquelctl builder check
.PP
Check that the build machine answers now.
.PP
The daemon otherwise checks it before each build, and \fBpiquelctl status\fR shows the latest check. Fails when the host has no build machine. Needs \fBsystem:operate\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl builder check\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl app
.PP
Create, inspect, edit and deploy applications.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app create\fR
Create an empty application.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service\fR
Add, change and remove an application\*(Aqs services.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app file\fR
List, add and remove the read\-only files services mount.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app volume\fR
Declare and remove named volumes.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app route\fR
Add, change and remove HTTPS routes and redirects.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app job\fR
Add, reorder and remove the jobs that run before each rollout.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app export\fR
Let other applications reach this application\*(Aqs services privately.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app import\fR
Reach the services other applications export, as \fB<service>.<application>\fR.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app variable\fR
Set and remove manifest variables, and their values per environment and for previews.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository\fR
Connect the application to a manifest in Git, and manage that connection.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app list\fR
List applications with their environments and status.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app show\fR
Show an application and its environments.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app logs\fR
Show recent Docker logs of the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app exec\fR
Run a one\-off command in a running task of a service.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret\fR
Declare the secrets piqueld generates for each environment.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app secret\fR
Manage the application\*(Aqs stored secrets and who may mount them.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app validate\fR
Check a TOML manifest locally, without contacting a daemon.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app plan\fR
Show what saving a TOML manifest would change, without saving it.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app apply\fR
Save a TOML manifest, creating or replacing the application it names.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app delete\fR
Delete an application with all its environments and previews.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app reconcile\fR
Retry the latest operation of the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app stop\fR
Stop the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app start\fR
Start the application\*(Aqs only environment again.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app deploy\fR
Deploy the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app rename\fR
Rename an application.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app manifest\fR
Print the saved manifest as TOML.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app releases\fR
List the application\*(Aqs releases, newest first.
.SS
piquelctl app create
.PP
Create an empty application.
.PP
Add services, volumes and routes to it with the other \fBapp\fR commands. Needs \fBapps:create\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app create\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Name of the new application, unused by any other.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SS
piquelctl app service
.PP
Add, change and remove an application\*(Aqs services.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app service\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service add\fR
Add a service that runs an image, or builds a Git repository with \fB\-\-git\fR.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service remove\fR
Remove a service.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service rename\fR
Rename a service.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service replicas\fR
Set the number of replicas the service runs.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service source\fR
Set where the service\*(Aqs image comes from: a prebuilt image or a Git build.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service env\fR
Set or remove one environment variable of a service.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service command\fR
Replace the image\*(Aqs entrypoint with the elements after \fB\-\-\fR.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service arguments\fR
Replace the image\*(Aqs default arguments with the elements after \fB\-\-\fR.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service depends\-on\fR
Set the services that must be healthy before this one rolls out.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service rollout\fR
Set the order and monitor window of the service\*(Aqs rollouts.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service telemetry\fR
Choose whether the service receives the daemon\*(Aqs own telemetry.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service security\fR
Harden the service\*(Aqs containers and its jobs\*(Aq.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service mount\fR
Mount a volume into a service, or remove a mount.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service secret\fR
Mount a secret into a service as a file, or remove a mount.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service health\fR
Set, change, or remove a service\*(Aqs health check.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service cpu\fR
Set the service\*(Aqs CPU limit, or remove it with \fB\-\-clear\fR.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app service memory\fR
Set the service\*(Aqs memory limit, or remove it with \fB\-\-clear\fR.
.SS
piquelctl app service add
.PP
Add a service that runs an image, or builds a Git repository with \fB\-\-git\fR.
.PP
The new service runs one replica and has no other settings. Adding a service whose name is taken fails.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app service add\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <SERVICE> [IMAGE]
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<SERVICE>\fR
Service name.
.TP
\fI[IMAGE]\fR
Image to run, such as \fBnginx:stable\fR. It may reference variables. Omit it when you pass \fB\-\-git\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-git\fR \fI<URL|self>\fR
Build this Git repository with Docker instead of running an image. It takes a clone URL, a path on the daemon\*(Aqs host, or \fBself\fR: the manifest\*(Aqs own repository, at the commit the manifest was read from.
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Branch to build when no commit is pinned. Default: \fBmain\fR. \fBself\fR doesn\*(Aqt take one.
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fI<COMMIT>\fR
Build this full commit hash instead of the branch head. \fBself\fR doesn\*(Aqt take one.
.TP
\fB\-\-dockerfile\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
