.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-seconds\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Seconds the job may run before it fails the deployment, from 1 to 86400. By default, the job\*(Aqs current timeout, or 300 for a new job.
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\-access\fR \fI<ACCESS>\fR
How the job mounts its service\*(Aqs volumes. By default, the job\*(Aqs current access, or \fBread\-only\fR for a new job.
.RS
.TP
\fBread\-only\fR
Mount every volume read\-only, so the job runs beside the services.
.TP
\fBexclusive\fR
Keep writable volumes writable, and stop every service that mounts one until the rollout.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\-service\fR \fI<on|off>\fR
\fBon\fR to stop the job\*(Aqs service before the job runs, once its startup dependencies are ready, until the rollout; \fBoff\fR to run it beside the service. By default, the job\*(Aqs current setting, or \fBoff\fR for a new job. Values: \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR.
