Change the variable\*(Aqs value in every preview, \fB[spec.previews.variables]\fR, instead of its default.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-string\fR
Keep the value as text even when it looks like a boolean or an integer.
.SS
piquelctl app variable unset
.PP
Remove a variable\*(Aqs default value, or its value in one environment or in previews.
.PP
Removing a value that isn\*(Aqt set fails.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app variable unset\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <NAME>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Variable name, referenced as \fB${{ vars.<name> }}\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Change the variable\*(Aqs value in this environment instead of its default. The environment must exist.
.TP
\fB\-\-previews\fR
Change the variable\*(Aqs value in every preview, \fB[spec.previews.variables]\fR, instead of its default.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app repository
.PP
Connect the application to a manifest in Git, and manage that connection.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository connect\fR
Connect the application to a manifest file in a Git repository.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository disconnect\fR
Stop reading the manifest from Git, keeping the saved manifest.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository url\fR
Change the repository every environment fetches the manifest from.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository path\fR
Change the manifest file every environment reads.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository sync\fR
Choose whether environments and previews deploy pushes.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository reset\fR
Discard the edits made since the manifest was last read from the repository, saving that manifest again.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository webhook\fR
Show the GitHub webhook that reports pushes, or generate its secret.
.SS
piquelctl app repository connect
.PP
Connect the application to a manifest file in a Git repository.
.PP
Deployments then fetch the manifest from the repository. Every environment follows \fB\-\-branch\fR, as do environments created later without their own, unless the manifest declares the environment\*(Aqs branch. Change an environment\*(Aqs branch with \fBenv branch\fR. You can still edit the application: deployments of the connection\*(Aqs branch deploy your edits until a push changes the manifest file.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository connect\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <URL> <PATH>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<URL>\fR
Git clone URL, or a path on the daemon\*(Aqs host.
.TP
\fI<PATH>\fR
Path of the manifest file, relative to the repository root.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Branch the environments follow. Default: \fBmain\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fI<COMMIT>\fR
Pin this full commit hash instead of following the branch.
.TP
\fB\-\-sync\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Whether to deploy pushes, as \fBapp repository sync\fR sets it. Default: \fBoff\fR.
.RS
.TP
\fBoff\fR
Deploy only when asked.
.TP
\fBpoll\fR
List the branches every \fB\-\-interval\fR seconds.
.TP
\fBwebhook\fR
List the branches when GitHub reports a push (see \fBapp repository webhook\fR).
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Seconds between polls with \fB\-\-sync poll\fR, from 60 to 86400. By default, 300.
.SS
piquelctl app repository disconnect
.PP
Stop reading the manifest from Git, keeping the saved manifest.
.PP
Edits are kept, and environments that followed a branch deploy the saved manifest. Declared environments lose their \fBbranch\fR, \fBcommit\fR and \fBsync\fR. It fails while services mount files from the repository: give them inline content first.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository disconnect\fR [OPTIONS] <APP>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app repository url
.PP
Change the repository every environment fetches the manifest from.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository url\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <URL>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<URL>\fR
Git clone URL, or a path on the daemon\*(Aqs host.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app repository path
.PP
Change the manifest file every environment reads.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository path\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <PATH>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<PATH>\fR
Path of the manifest file, relative to the repository root.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app repository sync
.PP
Choose whether environments and previews deploy pushes.
.PP
While sync is on, every preview, and every environment that opted in with \fBenv sync\fR and follows an unpinned branch, redeploys when its branch moves past the head of its last deployment.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository sync\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <MODE>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<MODE>\fR
How to detect pushes.
.RS
.TP
\fBoff\fR
Deploy only when asked.
.TP
\fBpoll\fR
List the branches every \fB\-\-interval\fR seconds.
.TP
\fBwebhook\fR
List the branches when GitHub reports a push (see \fBapp repository webhook\fR).
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Seconds between polls with \fBpoll\fR, from 60 to 86400. By default, 300.
.SS
piquelctl app repository reset
.PP
Discard the edits made since the manifest was last read from the repository, saving that manifest again.
.PP
\fBapp show\fR lists the edits. Deployments of the connection\*(Aqs branch then deploy the manifest as read, until a push changes it.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository reset\fR [OPTIONS] <APP>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app repository webhook
.PP
Show the GitHub webhook that reports pushes, or generate its secret.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository webhook\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository webhook show\fR
Show the payload URL to configure in GitHub, and when the secret was generated.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app repository webhook rotate\fR
Generate a new webhook secret, replacing the previous one, and print it.
.SS
piquelctl app repository webhook show
.PP
Show the payload URL to configure in GitHub, and when the secret was generated.
.PP
The URL appears once the daemon sets \fBingress.webhook_hostname\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository webhook show\fR [OPTIONS] <APP>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.SS
piquelctl app repository webhook rotate
.PP
Generate a new webhook secret, replacing the previous one, and print it.
.PP
The previous secret stops working at once. The new one is shown only this time.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app repository webhook rotate\fR [OPTIONS] <APP>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app list
.PP
List applications with their environments and status.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app list\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl app show
.PP
Show an application and its environments.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app show\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.SS
piquelctl app logs
.PP
Show recent Docker logs of the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.PP
With several environments, use \fBenv logs\fR. Needs \fBlogs:read\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app logs\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-service\fR \fI<SERVICE>\fR
Only show this service\*(Aqs output.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to every service.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-tail\fR \fI<TAIL>\fR
Show at most this many of the most recent lines, from 1 to 1000, merged across services. Default: \fB200\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-since\-seconds\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Only show output written within this many seconds, from 1 to 86400 (a day). Default: \fB3600\fR.
.SS
piquelctl app exec
.PP
Run a one\-off command in a running task of a service.
.PP
The command shares the task\*(Aqs image, environment, secrets, mounts and networks. Its output streams to your terminal, and \fBpiquelctl\fR exits with its exit code. Stopping \fBpiquelctl\fR early closes the stream, but the command may keep running. \fB\-\-timeout\fR limits connecting, not the session. Needs \fBapps:exec\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app exec\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID> <SERVICE> \-\- <COMMAND>...
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<SERVICE>\fR
Service that runs the command, in one of its running tasks.
.TP
\fI<COMMAND>...\fR
Program to run and its arguments, after \fB\-\-\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Environment name or stable ID.
.RS
.PP
Optional when the application has only one.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Forward standard input to the command.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tty\fR
Allocate a terminal, for interactive programs such as a shell.
.RS
.PP
It implies \fB\-\-interactive\fR, and needs a terminal on standard input, which it switches to raw mode so that keys such as Ctrl\-C reach the command.
.RE
.SS
piquelctl app generated\-secret
.PP
Declare the secrets piqueld generates for each environment.
.PP
These commands edit \fBspec.secrets\fR. Changing or removing a declaration keeps values already generated; replace one with \fBenv secret regenerate\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret list\fR
List the secrets the application declares for piqueld to generate, as saved.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret set\fR
Declare a secret piqueld generates, or replace how it is generated.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret remove\fR
Remove a declaration.
.SS
piquelctl app generated\-secret list
.PP
List the secrets the application declares for piqueld to generate, as saved.
.PP
\fBenv secret list\fR shows the values generated in each environment.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret list\fR [OPTIONS] <APP>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.SS
piquelctl app generated\-secret set
.PP
Declare a secret piqueld generates, or replace how it is generated.
.PP
Give exactly one of \fB\-\-bytes\fR or \fB\-\-rsa\-bits\fR. Values already generated are kept; \fBenv secret regenerate\fR replaces them.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret set\fR [OPTIONS] <\-\-bytes <BYTES>|\-\-rsa\-bits <RSA_BITS>> <APP> <NAME>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Secret name, as services and jobs mount it.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-bytes\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
Generate this many random bytes (16–512), encoded as text.
.TP
\fB\-\-encoding\fR \fI<ENCODING>\fR
Text encoding of the random bytes.
.RS
.PP
By default, \fBhex\fR.
.TP
\fBhex\fR
Lowercase hexadecimal, two characters per byte.
.TP
\fBbase64url\fR
URL\-safe base64 without padding.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rsa\-bits\fR \fI<RSA_BITS>\fR
Generate an RSA private key of this many bits (2048, 3072, or 4096) in PKCS#8 PEM.
.SS
piquelctl app generated\-secret remove
.PP
Remove a declaration.
.PP
Values already generated are kept. Removing a name the application doesn\*(Aqt declare fails.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app generated\-secret remove\fR [OPTIONS] <APP> <NAME>
.TP
\fI<APP>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Secret name, as services and jobs mount it.
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl app secret
.PP
Manage the application\*(Aqs stored secrets and who may mount them.
.PP
Values are write\-only: no command prints them back.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app secret\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <COMMAND>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app secret list\fR
List the application\*(Aqs stored secrets and who may mount them.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app secret set\fR
Create or replace a stored secret.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app secret access\fR
Change which environments, and whether previews, may mount a stored secret.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl app secret delete\fR
Delete a stored secret and the Docker secrets made from it.
.SS
piquelctl app secret list
.PP
List the application\*(Aqs stored secrets and who may mount them.
.PP
It shows each secret\*(Aqs version, never its value.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app secret\fR <APPLICATION> \fBlist\fR [OPTIONS]
.SS
piquelctl app secret set
.PP
Create or replace a stored secret.
.PP
The value, of 1 to 512000 bytes, comes from a file or standard input, never from an argument. Running services keep their value until the next deployment. A new secret may be mounted by every environment and no preview, unless you set its access. Needs \fBsecrets:write\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app secret\fR <APPLICATION> \fBset\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Secret name.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the value from this file.
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
Read the value from standard input, dropping one trailing newline. A terminal asks for it without echo.
.TP
\fB\-\-environments\fR \fI<ENVIRONMENTS>\fR
Let only these environments mount the secret: comma\-separated names or IDs, or \fB\*(Aq\*(Aq\fR for none.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-environments\fR
Let every environment mount the secret, including ones created later.
.RS
.PP
It never includes previews.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-previews\fR
Let previews mount the secret.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-previews\fR
Stop previews from mounting the secret.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the secret is at this generation; \fB0\fR requires that it doesn\*(Aqt exist.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to the generation it inspects, or \fB0\fR for a new secret.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SS
piquelctl app secret access
.PP
Change which environments, and whether previews, may mount a stored secret.
.PP
Options you omit keep the current access. Deployments that mount a secret they may no longer use fail with \fBsecret_access_denied\fR; running ones keep their value. Needs \fBsecrets:write\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app secret\fR <APPLICATION> \fBaccess\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Secret name.
.TP
\fB\-\-environments\fR \fI<ENVIRONMENTS>\fR
Let only these environments mount the secret: comma\-separated names or IDs, or \fB\*(Aq\*(Aq\fR for none.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-environments\fR
Let every environment mount the secret, including ones created later.
.RS
.PP
It never includes previews.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-previews\fR
Let previews mount the secret.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-previews\fR
Stop previews from mounting the secret.
.SS
piquelctl app secret delete
.PP
Delete a stored secret and the Docker secrets made from it.
.PP
It fails while any environment\*(Aqs configuration or deployment still uses the secret. Needs \fBsecrets:write\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app secret\fR <APPLICATION> \fBdelete\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Secret name.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the secret is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to the generation it inspects.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.SS
piquelctl app validate
.PP
Check a TOML manifest locally, without contacting a daemon.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app validate\fR [OPTIONS] \-\-file <PATH>
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Manifest file: UTF\-8 TOML of at most 2 MiB. Required.
.SS
piquelctl app plan
.PP
Show what saving a TOML manifest would change, without saving it.
.PP
It exits with code 3 when the plan is blocked.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app plan\fR [OPTIONS] \-\-file <PATH>
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Manifest file: UTF\-8 TOML of at most 2 MiB. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation; \fB0\fR requires that it doesn\*(Aqt exist.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Render the manifest for this environment, and compare it with that environment\*(Aqs deployment.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to the application\*(Aqs only environment. With several, the plan compares the manifest as written.
.RE
.SS
piquelctl app apply
.PP
Save a TOML manifest, creating or replacing the application it names.
.PP
Without \fB\-\-deploy\fR, it only saves the manifest. With it, it also deploys every environment that builds, and waits for each deployment.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app apply\fR [OPTIONS] \-\-file <PATH>
.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Manifest file: UTF\-8 TOML of at most 2 MiB. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation; \fB0\fR requires that it doesn\*(Aqt exist.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to the generation it inspects, or \fB0\fR when no application has the manifest\*(Aqs name.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace whichever application has the manifest\*(Aqs name now, or create it.
.RS
.PP
It skips the generation and identity checks, but still asks for confirmation.
