\fBpiquelctl app reconcile\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl app stop
.PP
Stop the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.PP
Its routes are withdrawn and its services scale to zero, until it is started, reconciled or deployed again. With several environments, use \fBenv stop\fR. Needs \fBapps:deploy\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app stop\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl app start
.PP
Start the application\*(Aqs only environment again.
.PP
Like \fBapp reconcile\fR, it retries the latest operation with its saved inputs. With several environments, use \fBenv start\fR. Needs \fBapps:deploy\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app start\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl app deploy
.PP
Deploy the application\*(Aqs only environment.
.PP
It fetches the manifest again, from the environment\*(Aqs branch for a repository\-backed application, and resolves images and Git sources again. With several environments, use \fBenv deploy\fR. Needs \fBapps:deploy\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app deploy\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Fetch the repository manifest from this branch, for this deployment only.
.RS
.PP
The environment keeps following its own branch.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fI<SHA>\fR
Fetch the repository manifest at this full commit hash, for this deployment only.
.TP
\fB\-\-rebuild\fR
Build every service\*(Aqs image from Git again.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a service whose commit and build settings an earlier build of the application already built reuses that build\*(Aqs image. A rebuild also pulls newer base images.
