\fBpiquelctl app manifest\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.SS
piquelctl app releases
.PP
List the application\*(Aqs releases, newest first.
.PP
A release records what a deployment prepared: the manifest, and each service\*(Aqs image and where it came from.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl app releases\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME_OR_ID>
.TP
\fI<NAME_OR_ID>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fI<CURSOR>\fR
Read the page after this cursor, which the previous page printed.
.SS
piquelctl env
.PP
Create, inspect, deploy and delete an application\*(Aqs environments.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env\fR [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env list\fR
List an application\*(Aqs environments and their status.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env create\fR
Add an environment to an application.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env source\fR
Make an environment receive releases promoted from another one, or build its own source again.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env promote\fR
Deploy a release into a promoted environment without building it.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env branch\fR
Point an environment at another branch of the manifest repository, or pin or unpin its commit.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env sync\fR
Choose whether pushes to an environment\*(Aqs branch deploy it.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env telemetry\fR
Grant an environment the daemon\*(Aqs telemetry, or revoke it.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env show\fR
Show one environment, the manifest it deploys, and its status.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env visibility\fR
Cap the visibility of an environment\*(Aqs routes in the saved manifest.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env rollback\fR
Choose what happens when an environment\*(Aqs rollout fails.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env rename\fR
Rename an environment without redeploying it.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env delete\fR
Delete an environment, keeping its named volumes.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env deploy\fR
Deploy an environment from its source.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env reconcile\fR
Retry an environment\*(Aqs latest operation with the inputs it was given.
.TP
