Stop an environment, keeping its configuration, volumes and secrets.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env start\fR
Start a stopped environment again.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env secret\fR
List, regenerate, or delete an environment\*(Aqs generated secrets.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env logs\fR
Print the most recent lines of an environment\*(Aqs Docker logs.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env history\fR
List an environment\*(Aqs deployments, newest first: each one\*(Aqs outcome, where it came from, and its release.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env attempts\fR
List the attempts of one of an environment\*(Aqs deployments, newest first: each try at rolling it out, how it ended, and when it last changed.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env restore\fR
Deploy an earlier, succeeded deployment again exactly as it ran: its rendered manifest, images and pinned secret versions. Jobs don\*(Aqt run, and volume contents and migrations stay as they are.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env wait\fR
Wait until a deployment of an environment is ready.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env url\fR
Print the URLs of an environment\*(Aqs routes, and whether each is ready.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl env traffic\fR
Show how many people visit an environment, and the requests its routes served, over a time window.
.SS
piquelctl env list
.PP
List an application\*(Aqs environments and their status.
.PP
Previews are not listed; use \fBpreview list\fR for them.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env list\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.SS
piquelctl env create
.PP
Add an environment to an application.
.PP
Nothing is deployed until you run \fBenv deploy\fR, or \fBenv promote\fR for a promoted environment. The environment deploys the application\*(Aqs saved manifest or, when the application is repository\-backed, the manifest on its own branch.
.PP
You can\*(Aqt create an environment that the saved manifest has a \fB[spec.environments.<name>]\fR block for: saving the manifest creates it.
