.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Branch of the manifest repository the environment follows. By default, the branch \fBspec.manifest\fR names. Only for repository\-backed applications.
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fI<SHA>\fR
Deploy this commit of \fB\-\-branch\fR instead of the branch\*(Aqs head: a full commit hash of 40 or 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
.TP
\fB\-\-promote\-from\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Make the environment promoted: it never builds, and only receives releases promoted from this environment of the application, given by name or stable ID, with \fBenv promote\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Change the environment only if the application\*(Aqs generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the command.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Change the environment even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.SS
piquelctl env source
.PP
Make an environment receive releases promoted from another one, or build its own source again.
.PP
Nothing is deployed. A promoted environment never builds: it deploys what \fBenv promote\fR sends it. When the saved manifest sets the environment\*(Aqs \fBpromote_from\fR, \fBbranch\fR, \fBcommit\fR or \fBsync\fR, change it there instead.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env source\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <ENVIRONMENT>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<ENVIRONMENT>\fR
Environment name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-promote\-from\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Receive releases promoted from this environment of the application, given by name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-tracking\fR
Stop receiving promoted releases and build again: the saved manifest, or the branch \fBspec.manifest\fR names. Use \fBenv branch\fR afterwards to follow another branch.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Change the environment only if the application\*(Aqs generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the command.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Change the environment even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.SS
piquelctl env promote
.PP
Deploy a release into a promoted environment without building it.
.PP
By default, it deploys the release of the source environment\*(Aqs current deployment, which must have succeeded and be healthy now. The command asks for confirmation and waits for the deployment.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env promote\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <ENVIRONMENT>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<ENVIRONMENT>\fR
