.TP
\fB\-\-deployment\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Promote the release of this deployment of the source environment. The command fails if it is no longer the source\*(Aqs current deployment.
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Deploy this earlier release of the application instead, with the environment\*(Aqs current secrets.
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR
Show what would be deployed, and any secret it can\*(Aqt use, without deploying. The command exits with code 3 if the promotion would be refused. With \fB\-\-release\fR, you can plan for any environment, promoted or not.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Promote even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl env branch
.PP
Point an environment at another branch of the manifest repository, or pin or unpin its commit.
.PP
Only for repository\-backed applications. Nothing is deployed: the environment\*(Aqs next deployment fetches the manifest from the new branch or commit. A promoted environment has no branch; use \fBenv source \-\-tracking\fR first. When the saved manifest sets the environment\*(Aqs \fBbranch\fR, \fBcommit\fR, \fBpromote_from\fR or \fBsync\fR, change it there instead.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env branch\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <ENVIRONMENT> <BRANCH>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<ENVIRONMENT>\fR
Environment name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<BRANCH>\fR
Branch of the manifest repository the environment follows.
.TP
\fB\-\-commit\fR \fI<SHA>\fR
Deploy this commit of the branch instead of the branch\*(Aqs head: a full commit hash of 40 or 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters. Without it, the environment follows the branch\*(Aqs head, unpinning any commit.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Change the environment only if the application\*(Aqs generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the command.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Change the environment even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.SS
piquelctl env sync
.PP
Choose whether pushes to an environment\*(Aqs branch deploy it.
.PP
This applies while the application\*(Aqs repository syncs (\fBapp repository sync\fR). An environment that opts in deploys again whenever its branch moves past the head of its last deployment; one never deployed starts following from its first deployment. A pinned commit never follows pushes. When the saved manifest sets the environment\*(Aqs \fBsync\fR, \fBbranch\fR, \fBcommit\fR or \fBpromote_from\fR, change it there instead. Opting in while the repository syncs needs the \fBapps:deploy\fR permission too.
