\fBpiquelctl env sync\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <ENVIRONMENT> <on|off>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<ENVIRONMENT>\fR
Environment name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<on|off>\fR
\fBon\fR deploys the environment when its branch moves; \fBoff\fR deploys it only when you ask. Values: \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR.
.SS
piquelctl env telemetry
.PP
Grant an environment the daemon\*(Aqs telemetry, or revoke it.
.PP
The receiving service of a granted environment, marked with \fBapp service telemetry\fR, gets the traces, metrics and logs of every application. Revoking stops the export at once. Either way, the daemon mounts or unmounts the telemetry socket within seconds, which restarts the service; nothing is deployed. Both need the \fBtelemetry:grant\fR permission. Previews are never granted.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env telemetry\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <ENVIRONMENT> <on|off>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<ENVIRONMENT>\fR
Environment name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<on|off>\fR
\fBon\fR grants the environment every application\*(Aqs telemetry; \fBoff\fR revokes it. Values: \fBon\fR, \fBoff\fR.
.SS
piquelctl env show
.PP
Show one environment, the manifest it deploys, and its status.
