.TP
\fB\-\-deploy\fR
Also deploy the saved configuration to each declared environment that isn\*(Aqt promoted from another.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the change is saved, or its deployments accepted, without waiting for them to end.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Save only if the application\*(Aqs saved generation is still \fBGENERATION\fR. By default, it must still be the generation the command read, so a concurrent change fails the save instead of being overwritten.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Save even if the application changed since the command read it. It still asks for confirmation.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt. You need it when not on a terminal.
.SS
piquelctl env rollback
.PP
Choose what happens when an environment\*(Aqs rollout fails.
.PP
A rollout fails when Docker pauses a service update because a new container failed within its monitor window. With \fBautomatic\fR, piqueld then restores the environment\*(Aqs last successful deployment, like \fBenv restore\fR; with \fBmanual\fR, the environment stays degraded until you deploy or restore. \fBdefault\fR is automatic for promoted environments and manual for the others. The setting is saved in the environment\*(Aqs \fB[spec.environments.<name>]\fR block. Data is never reverted.
