If the operation is still in progress, the command waits for it instead of starting it again. A stopped environment starts.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env reconcile\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> [ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI[ENVIRONMENT]\fR
Environment name or stable ID. You can omit it when the application has exactly one environment.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl env stop
.PP
Stop an environment, keeping its configuration, volumes and secrets.
.PP
Its routes are withdrawn and its services scale to zero. It stays stopped until \fBenv start\fR, \fBenv reconcile\fR, a deployment, a restore or a promotion into it; pushes don\*(Aqt deploy it meanwhile. The command asks for confirmation and waits until its services have stopped. Previews are deleted instead.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env stop\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> [ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI[ENVIRONMENT]\fR
Environment name or stable ID. You can omit it when the application has exactly one environment.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl env start
.PP
Start a stopped environment again.
.PP
Its services run their replicas again and its routes are served. Like \fBenv reconcile\fR, it retries the latest operation with the inputs it was given, or waits for it while it is in progress.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env start\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> [ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI[ENVIRONMENT]\fR
Environment name or stable ID. You can omit it when the application has exactly one environment.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the application is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Without it, a deployment uses the generation it inspects, and a retry checks none.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the operation, without waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl env secret
