It fails while the configuration or a deployment still uses the secret. A later deployment that mounts it generates a new value. Needs \fBsecrets:write\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl env secret delete\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> <ENVIRONMENT> <NAME>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<ENVIRONMENT>\fR
Environment name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI<NAME>\fR
Secret name.
.TP
\fB\-\-expected\-generation\fR \fI<GENERATION>\fR
Fail unless the secret is at this generation.
.RS
.PP
Defaults to the generation it inspects.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt.
