.SS
piquelctl preview create
.PP
Create a preview of a branch and deploy it.
.PP
Only for repository\-backed applications. If the preview of that branch and slot already exists, the command shows it and its latest deployment without deploying it again. It fails when a new preview would exceed the daemon\*(Aqs preview limits.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl preview create\fR [OPTIONS] \-\-branch <BRANCH> <APPLICATION>
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Branch of the manifest repository to deploy. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot\fR \fI<SLOT>\fR
Distinguishes several previews of one branch, such as one per agent: 1 to 63 lowercase letters, digits, or hyphens, starting with a letter and ending with a letter or digit.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the deployment, without waiting for it to finish.
.SS
piquelctl preview deploy
.PP
Deploy the head of a preview\*(Aqs branch again, or a snapshot of your Git worktree with \fB\-\-local\fR.
.PP
Deploying the branch\*(Aqs head replaces a local snapshot the preview runs.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl preview deploy\fR [OPTIONS] <APPLICATION> [PREVIEW]
.TP
\fI<APPLICATION>\fR
Application name or stable ID.
.TP
\fI[PREVIEW]\fR
Preview ID, slug, or branch. Omit it with \fB\-\-local\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot\fR \fI<SLOT>\fR
The preview\*(Aqs slot. Give it to address a preview with a slot by its branch, or to choose the preview \fB\-\-local\fR deploys to.
.TP
\fB\-\-local\fR
Deploy a snapshot of the Git worktree of the current directory, without pushing it.
.RS
.PP
The snapshot has the worktree\*(Aqs committed, uncommitted, and untracked files. Ignored files are left out, or sent as committed when they are tracked. The command lists the uncommitted files it sends, and deploys to the preview of the current branch and \fB\-\-slot\fR, creating it if needed. Your repository is never changed. A large first upload may need a longer \fB\-\-timeout\fR.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-history\fR
Upload every commit of \fBHEAD\fR with the snapshot.
.RS
.PP
By default, the command sends only the commits since the nearest ancestor of \fBHEAD\fR that a remote\-tracking branch has, and the daemon fetches that ancestor from the application\*(Aqs repository. Use this when there is no such ancestor, or the daemon can\*(Aqt fetch it.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Deploy the snapshot as the preview of this branch instead of the current one. Required when \fBHEAD\fR is detached.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-secret\-files\fR
Send files not in \fBHEAD\fR whose names usually hold credentials too.
.RS
.PP
Without it, \fB\-\-local\fR refuses to send an untracked or only staged \fB.env*\fR file (but \fB.example\fR, \fB.sample\fR and \fB.template\fR ones), SSH key \fBid_*\fR, \fB*.pem\fR, \fB*.key\fR, \fB*.p12\fR or \fB*.pfx\fR file, \fBcredentials\fR or \fB*credentials.json\fR, \fB.npmrc\fR, \fB.pypirc\fR, \fB.netrc\fR or \fB.git\-credentials\fR, in any case. Ignore such files in \fB.gitignore\fR instead when the preview doesn\*(Aqt need them.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Return once the daemon accepts the deployment, without waiting for it to finish.
