List Git source builds and job runs, newest first.
.TP
\fBpiquelctl build logs\fR
Read the newest page of a build\*(Aqs output.
.SS
piquelctl build list
.PP
List Git source builds and job runs, newest first.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl build list\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR \fI<APP>\fR
Only this application and its environments, by name or ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Only this environment or preview: with \fB\-\-app\fR, an environment by name or ID, or a preview by ID. Alone, it takes only an ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fI<CURSOR>\fR
Read the page after this cursor, which the previous page printed.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Show at most this many items, from 1 to 100. Default: \fB50\fR.
.SS
piquelctl build logs
.PP
Read the newest page of a build\*(Aqs output.
.PP
To read older output, pass the \fB\-\-before\fR offset it prints. Needs \fBlogs:read\fR.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl build logs\fR [OPTIONS] <ID>
.TP
\fI<ID>\fR
Build ID, from \fBbuild list\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-before\fR \fI<OFFSET>\fR
Read the output before this byte offset, which the previous page printed.
.SS
piquelctl operation
.PP
Show an operation, waiting until it ends.
.PP
Deployments, deletions and other long tasks run as operations, whose IDs commands print. Unless you pass \fB\-\-no\-wait\fR, it exits with code 5 if the operation failed.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl operation\fR [OPTIONS] <OPERATION_ID>
.TP
\fI<OPERATION_ID>\fR
Operation ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR
Show the operation\*(Aqs current state instead of waiting for it to end.
.SS
piquelctl analytics
.PP
Summarize deployment outcomes, retries, durations, and failure codes over a time window, for every readable application or one environment.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl analytics\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR \fI<APP>\fR
Only deployments of this application\*(Aqs environment, by name or ID; every readable application\*(Aqs when omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
The environment of \-\-app, by name or ID; required when it has several.
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<SINCE>\fR
Start this long ago, such as 24h or 7d; defaults to 30 days before the end.
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<UNTIL>\fR
End this long ago; defaults to now.
.SS
piquelctl event
.PP
Read one page of the event history, newest first.
.PP
Events record what happened to applications, environments and the daemon, such as edits, deployments and failures. A deleted environment\*(Aqs events outlive it: find them with \fB\-\-env\fR and its ID.
.PP
\fBpiquelctl event\fR [OPTIONS]
.TP
\fB\-\-app\fR \fI<APP>\fR
Only this application and its environments, by name or ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Only this environment or preview: with \fB\-\-app\fR, an environment by name or ID, or a preview by ID. Alone, it takes only an ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
Only show events of this kind, such as \fBoperation_failed\fR.
.RS
.PP
The dashboard\*(Aqs Events page lists the kinds recorded so far.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-errors\-only\fR
Only show failures: events that carry an error code.
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fI<CURSOR>\fR
Read the page after this cursor, which the previous page printed.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Show at most this many items, from 1 to 100. Default: \fB50\fR.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command succeeded.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The command failed for a reason no other status names.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command line, its input or the connection\*(Aqs configuration is invalid, or you didn\*(Aqt confirm the action.
.TP
\fB3\fR
A conflict: a name matches more than one thing, a plan is blocked, someone else changed what the command edits, or a newer deployment replaced the one it waited for.
.TP
\fB4\fR
The daemon couldn\*(Aqt be reached or is overloaded, or the command ran out of time. Work the daemon had started goes on.
.TP
\fB5\fR
The operation the command waited for failed.
.TP
\fB6\fR
\fBdoctor\fR found a failed check, or \fBbuilder check\fR an unreachable build machine.
.TP
\fB7\fR
The daemon rejected the credential, or the credential lacks the access the command needs.
.TP
\fB130\fR
The command was interrupted, by Ctrl\-C, \fBSIGTERM\fR, or \fBSIGHUP\fR when its terminal closed.
.PP
\fBapp exec\fR and \fBpreview exec\fR exit with the status of the command they ran.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_PROFILE\fR
The connection profile to use, unless \fB\-\-profile\fR names one.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_PROFILES_FILE\fR
The only file to read profiles from, unless \fB\-\-profiles\-file\fR names one.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_SOCKET\fR
The path of the daemon\*(Aqs Unix socket, unless \fB\-\-socket\fR or \fB\-\-url\fR is given.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_URL\fR
The address of the daemon, over HTTP or HTTPS, unless \fB\-\-url\fR or \fB\-\-socket\fR is given.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_TOKEN\fR
An API token to authenticate with, instead of a saved login.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_CREDENTIALS_FILE\fR
The file that holds the saved logins.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_TIMEOUT\fR
How long a command may take, unless \fB\-\-timeout\fR says.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_WAIT_TIMEOUT\fR
How long a command waits for an operation, unless \fB\-\-wait\-timeout\fR says.
.TP
\fBPIQUELD_REQUEST_ID\fR
The ID \fB\-\-request\-id\fR takes, unless it is given.
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
The directory that holds \fBpiqueld/profiles.toml\fR and \fBpiqueld/credentials.json\fR, instead of \fB~/.config\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/run/piqueld/piqueld.sock\fR
The daemon\*(Aqs Unix socket, which \fBpiquelctl\fR connects to unless told otherwise.
.TP
\fB/etc/piqueld/profiles.toml\fR
The connection profiles of every user of the machine.
.TP
\fB~/.config/piqueld/profiles.toml\fR
Your connection profiles, which replace those of the same name.
.TP
\fB~/.config/piqueld/credentials.json\fR
The logins \fBpiquelctl login\fR saved, which only you can read.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBpiqueld\fR(8)
.PP
The documentation, at https://docs.piqueld.dev.
